• [0mUpdated the voice behavior:

  - Usually one or two short sentences.
  - Calls session operations immediately and silently.
  - No “let me check,” latency-filling, or repeated summaries.
  - Never mentions CLI, commands, arguments, tools, or confirmation mechanics.
  - Uses only session-oriented terminology.
  - Doesn’t speculate about [38;5;6munknown[39m states.
  - Unclear speech gets only: “Could you repeat that?”
  - Tool descriptions no longer expose approval details.

  The local terminal can still request confirmation for starting a session or forcing a follow-up, but the assistant won’t narrate it. Normal list, status, and follow-up operations require no confirmation.

  This follows official OpenAI guidance to keep prompts and tool descriptions lean, precise, and non-repetitive. ]8;;https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model\OpenAI model guidance]8;;\ ([4m[38;5;6m]8;;https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model\https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model[0m]8;;\)

